---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const TITLE = 'Library Reader — save, read, highlight, and listen';
const DESCRIPTION =
  'A personal research library for articles and PDFs. Clean typography, persistent highlights, text-to-speech, and AI chat over your own sources.';
---

<Layout title={TITLE} description={DESCRIPTION}>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="header">
      <div class="header-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
          <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">L</span>
          <span>Library Reader</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary">
          <a href="#features">Features</a>
          <a href="#how">How it works</a>
          <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>
          <a href="/extension">Extension</a>
          <a href="/changelog">Changelog</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="btn-signin" href="/login">Sign in</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">Personal research library</span>
          <h1>Save it, read it, highlight it, listen to it.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">
            One library for the articles and PDFs you actually want to read. Clean typography,
            persistent highlights, text-to-speech, and AI chat over your own sources.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn-primary" href="/library">
              Save your first article
              <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="fine">
            No account needed — works in your browser right now.
            <a href="/extension">Chrome extension available.</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="library-preview" aria-label="Illustrative Library Reader view">
          <div class="preview-head">
            <span>Illustrative library</span>
            <span>3 saved sources</span>
          </div>
          <div class="preview-body">
            <p class="preview-kicker">Continue reading</p>
            <h2>How durable systems earn trust</h2>
            <p class="preview-meta">Article · 14 min · 3 highlights</p>
            <blockquote>
              “The useful part is not collecting more material. It is keeping the evidence close
              enough to revisit.”
            </blockquote>
            <div class="preview-actions" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>Highlight</span><span>Add note</span><span>Listen</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="preview-note">Example content only — your library renders your saved sources.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="features" class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>What it actually does</h2>
        <p>Three things, kept deliberately small. No feed, no recommendations, no inbox.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
          <h3>One library for articles and PDFs</h3>
          <p>
            Paste a URL and the page is cleaned with Mozilla Readability. Upload a PDF and it goes
            into the same library, with text extraction for search and chat.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
          <h3>Highlight and annotate</h3>
          <p>
            A distraction-free reader view with persistent highlights and a side panel for notes.
            Annotations anchor to the exact text you marked so they survive across visits.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
          <h3>Listen to anything you save</h3>
          <p>
            Hit Listen on an article or PDF and your browser reads it aloud — voice and rate are
            controllable. The same control is available from the Chrome extension.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="demo" class="section section-bordered">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="section-head-inline"><span aria-hidden="true">✨</span> The reader view</h2>
        <p>
          Articles get cleaned into a typography-first layout. Select any text to add a note or send
          it to AI. Press the Listen button to have the page read aloud.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="demo-frame" aria-label="Reader layout sketch">
        <div class="demo-bar">
          <div class="demo-dots" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="demo-dot"></span>
            <span class="demo-dot"></span>
            <span class="demo-dot"></span>
          </div>
          <span>library / reader</span>
          <span class="demo-listen">🎧 Listen</span>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-grid">
          <div class="demo-main">
            <div class="demo-label">Article</div>
            <div class="skeleton-title"></div>
            <div class="skeleton-sub"></div>
            <div class="skeleton-lines">
              <div class="skeleton-line w97"></div>
              <div class="skeleton-line w94"></div>
              <div class="skeleton-line w60"></div>
              <div class="skeleton-line w88"></div>
              <div class="skeleton-line w92"></div>
              <div class="skeleton-line w40"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="demo-aside">
            <div class="demo-label">Notes</div>
            <div class="note-card">
              <div class="note-line w75"></div>
              <div class="note-line full"></div>
              <div class="note-line w80"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="note-card">
              <div class="note-line w50"></div>
              <div class="note-line full"></div>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="demo-caption">Layout sketch — your library renders your real content.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="how" class="section section-bordered">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>Three steps from a URL to a library you keep coming back to.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="step-num">1</div>
          <h3>Save a source</h3>
          <p>
            Paste a link, drop a PDF, or use the Chrome extension to capture the current page in one
            click.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="step-num">2</div>
          <h3>Read, highlight, listen</h3>
          <p>
            Open it in the reader view. Highlight what matters, add notes in the side panel, or play
            it back as audio.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="step-num">3</div>
          <h3>Ask and revisit</h3>
          <p>
            Generate a summary, chat with the text using your own AI key, and come back to your
            highlights any time.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="faq" class="faq">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <p class="faq-intro">
        A few common questions. <a href="/faq">See the full FAQ →</a>
      </p>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Do I need an account to try it?</summary>
          <p>
            No. The library works in your browser without signing in — articles, PDFs, highlights,
            and notes are stored locally. Sign in with Google when you want to sync across devices.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Where are my PDFs stored?</summary>
          <p>
            For signed-in users, PDFs are uploaded to Cloudflare R2 and accessed through a proxy
            that enforces ownership. In local mode, the PDF stays in your browser.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How does the AI chat work? Whose API key does it use?</summary>
          <p>
            You bring your own key — OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini — and it is stored in your
            browser. There is also a gateway option and a local-AI mode for development. We never
            proxy your key through a server.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What does the Chrome extension do?</summary>
          <p>
            It captures the page you are on (cleaned via Readability) and saves it to your library.
            It also exposes the Listen control, so you can have any page read aloud without leaving
            it.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Can I export my data?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. The About page has an Export button that downloads every article, board, and list
            scoped to your account as a single JSON file.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing">
      <div class="closing-inner">
        <h2>Start your library</h2>
        <p>
          Save your first article or PDF. It works in your browser right now — sign in later if you
          want to sync.
        </p>
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/library">
          Save your first article
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <p class="footer-links">
          <a href="/about">About</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> ·
          <a href="/extension">Chrome extension</a> · <a href="/changelog">Changelog</a> ·
          <a href="https://github.com/Significant-Hobbies/reader/issues">Roadmap</a> ·
          <a href="https://github.com/Significant-Hobbies/reader">Source</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      Your reading list is not the same as your understanding. Library Reader helps with the gap.
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>
